        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Sangin, Helmand River, Lashkargah, Sistan Basin, Afghanistan\n- Infrastructure: Route 611\n- People: Hasti Gul Abid\n- Topics: geography, transportation, cricket\n\nFacts:\n- The Helmand River is the longest river in Afghanistan and the primary watershed for the endorheic Sistan Basin.\n- Sangin is located in the valley of the Helmand River at an altitude of 888 meters, 95 kilometers northeast of Lashkargah.\n- Route 611 in Afghanistan is approximately 100 kilometers long and passes through the town of Sangin.\n- Hasti Gul Abid, born on 1 January 1984, is an Afghan cricketer.",
